{
  "id": "ss.lib.dot-head",
  "name": "Dot's head",
  "description": "Dot's head, drawn on its own and large, to be composed into `ss.char.dot` by `use` at about a fifth of this size. Leather and cloth, nothing that shines but one buckle: Dot is the plain survivor, the one whose weapon is its own feelers, and it dresses like someone who walks a long way. From the neck up: the top of the mantle collar bound in leather and stitched; a wool scarf wound twice round the throat with its tail hanging frayed over the collar. A close leather coif over the skull, seamed and stitched across the crown, showing at the temple and the cheek, held by a chin strap with the buckle. The face is a shadow under the hood — a cloth wrap pulled up over it from the nose down, two folds in it, a lighter edge — with two cold glints where the eyes are and no skin anywhere. Over all of it a deep hood of heavy wool in a gradient from light at the crown to near-black at the hem, its opening bound in leather and stitched, worn pale along one crease, lined dark inside so the face sits back in it, the point trailing behind; a bone bead hangs on a cord from the rim. At the crown, two leather grommets that the feelers come through — the first inch of each is here; the long dead arcs that hang from them belong to the character document, where they can be animated.",
